   "beats": [
    {
     "en": "Copper is in your phone, your car, and every power line.",
     "jp": "銅は、スマホにも車にも、すべての電線にも入っています。",
     "hl": [
      "every power line",
      "すべての電線"
     ],
     "start": 0.6,
     "end": 3.809,
     "audio": "00_00.wav"
    },
    {
     "en": "In January 2026, its price briefly went above 14,500 dollars a tonne.",
     "jp": "2026年1月、その価格は一時1トン1万4500ドルを超えました。",
     "hl": [
      "14,500 dollars",
      "1万4500ドル"
     ],
     "start": 4.459,
     "end": 10.89,
     "audio": "00_01.wav"
    },
    {
     "en": "Only a month earlier, it had passed 12,000 dollars for the first time.",
     "jp": "そのわずか1か月前に、初めて1万2000ドルを超えたばかりでした。",
     "hl": [
      "for the first time",
      "初めて"
     ],
     "start": 11.54,
     "end": 15.815,
     "audio": "00_02.wav"
    },
    {
     "en": "Today: why copper is so tight, and what it means for Japan.",
     "jp": "今日は、銅がなぜこれほど足りないのか、日本にどう関係するのかを見ます。",
     "hl": [
      "so tight",
      "足りない"
     ],
     "start": 16.465,
     "end": 19.851,
     "audio": "00_03.wav"
    }
   ],
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 20.851
  },
  {
   "id": "demand",
   "chapter": "WHO WANTS IT?",
   "vis": {
    "type": "flow",
    "title": "Electrification needs copper",
    "title_jp": "電化には銅が要る",
    "items": [
     {
      "title": "Power grids",
      "jp": "送電網",
      "color": "navy"
     },
     {
      "title": "Electric cars",
      "jp": "電気自動車",
      "color": "navy"
     },
     {
      "title": "AI data centers",
      "jp": "AIデータセンター",
      "color": "navy"
     },
     {
      "title": "More copper",
      "jp": "銅の需要が増える",
      "color": "red"
     }
    ],
    "at": [
     0,
     1,
     2,
     3
    ]
   },
   "beats": [
    {
     "en": "Copper carries electricity better than almost any other metal.",
     "jp": "銅は、ほかのほとんどの金属より電気をよく通します。",
     "hl": [
      "carries electricity",
      "電気をよく通します"
     ],
     "start": 21.451,
     "end": 24.942,
     "audio": "01_00.wav"
    },
    {
     "en": "So the world needs more of it for power grids and electric cars.",
     "jp": "だから世界は、送電網や電気自動車のためにもっと銅を必要としています。",
     "hl": [
      "power grids",
      "送電網"
     ],
     "start": 25.592,
     "end": 29.318,
     "audio": "01_01.wav"
    },
    {
     "en": "The IEA also points to data centers and AI as new sources of demand.",
     "jp": "IEAは、データセンターとAIも新しい需要だと指摘しています。",
     "hl": [
      "new sources of demand",
      "新しい需要"
     ],
     "start": 29.968,
     "end": 34.968,
     "audio": "01_02.wav"
    },
    {
     "en": "Demand is expected to grow. The hard part is supply.",
     "jp": "需要は伸びる見通しです。難しいのは、供給のほうです。",
     "hl": [
      "The hard part",
      "難しいのは"
     ],
     "start": 35.618,
     "end": 39.026,
     "audio": "01_03.wav"
    }
